{"id":"beats-5b11b2","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-3dd84ecf-82f9-4b8d-9d75-014e525f2945","text":"## Summary\n\nDashboard now reads as a coherent, polished page that visually matches the Issues view. Everything from the original plan landed plus several iteration-driven refinements.\n\n## Structure (from the original plan)\n\n- **Full-width-ish layout** — `max-w-7xl mx-auto` instead of `max-w-6xl` centered. Section headers and rows span the same bound.\n- **`Section` helper component** — extracted to encapsulate header (icon + title + count), optional collapsible chevron with localStorage persistence, and section body.\n- **De-carded list sections** — Workload, Needs Attention, Active Epics, Recent Activity dropped their elevated `\u003cCard\u003e` wrappers and became inline lists under section headers.\n- **Section header treatment** — Issues-style `bg-secondary py-2 px-5` with small icon + plain-case name + muted count. Visually consistent with Backlog status groups.\n- **Page chrome** — top header matches Issues' h-11 border-b row, with right-side issue count via `ml-auto`.\n- **Pulse tiles tightened** — `padding=\"sm\"` + `min-h-[112px]`.\n- **Composition uses the same `Section` pattern** — no more bespoke chevron+border-t; just `collapsible defaultOpen={false}` with its storageKey.\n\n## Iteration-driven refinements\n\n- **Renamed to \"Overview\"** with a new stacked-rectangles icon — \"Dashboard\" felt generic, \"Overview\" matches the at-a-glance framing.\n- **Bumped `--color-text-muted`** from `#555` (3.4:1) to `#7a7a7d` (4.8:1, passes WCAG AA). Timestamps and action verbs in Recent Activity went from barely-visible to clearly de-emphasized.\n- **Comment activity** — preview now runs through a `stripMarkdown()` helper so `##`, `**`, backticks etc. don't appear as raw text. Click a comment row to expand inline into a lighter-bg box rendered as full markdown.\n- **All sections collapsible** — each with its own `storageKey` for individual persistence.\n- **Spacing tuned** — initially `space-y-0` with section borders felt too dense → settled on `space-y-3` + `py-3` on the parent, with section borders removed and `bg-secondary` headers carrying the visual delineation.\n- **Active Epics row** — matched the Backlog row format exactly: `StatusIcon → Title → CopyableId → (STALE?) → SubProgress + N/M`. Dropped the bar+% and points columns since the SubProgress ring already visualizes completion.\n- **Section reorder** — settled on Pulse → Needs Attention → Workload → Active Epics → Recent Activity → Composition.\n- **Needs Attention auto-hides** when there's nothing surfaced — no vestigial \"Nothing urgent\" placeholder eating vertical space.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `make frontend` builds cleanly throughout\n- Visually compared side-by-side with the Issues view — same chrome, same section-group rhythm, same density\n- All collapsible toggles persist across reload"},"created_at":"2026-05-26T15:06:11.779776022Z","created_by":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e"}
